Comments on Darkly Dreaming Dexter, by Jeff Lindsay
Posted by Mike Swope (Reviewer) on 2/25/2008
You make a good point. I do not cite any negatives in my review. None strike me as important enough to cite...petty things, IMHO. As the second commenter notes, these ratings things are arbitrary (no specified criteria for judgment). My rating for this book is a great rating...and after a few months, or year or more, if this book and its themes stick with me, then it would be a 10, as it has entered my life experience. There are only a few such books I've ever read. This one is likely to be one of them. But not yet. It's like fine wine. It may get better with age, though it is already very, very good. :)
Posted by Pete on 2/21/2008
Stars are not given on a point system -- they're an arbitrary (at best) judgement, and mean different things to different people.

Surely you've read a book which has been technically perfect, and pretty darn good to boot, but wouldn't necessarily make your list of most amazing books that rocked your world?
Posted by Anon on 2/20/2008
Why did this only get four starts out of five? No negatives are cited.
