A New Look Staveley MWFC Earn A Point Against Heanor. Match Report


Thursday 7th February 2013
Report by Jim McIntosh.
Pics courtesy Barry Dyke


Wednesday 6th February 2013
Staveley MWFC 1 - 1 Heanor Town
Baris NCEL Premier

A new era began at Inkersall Road on Wednesday night with a much changed team taking the field for Staveley after 12 first team players left the club, resulting in a number of reserve and youth team players being promoted to the first team.

Staveley took the lead with their first attack when Lee Growcock played Ryan Damms in, 'Dammsy' making no mistake with his accurate left foot shot.The attitude, work rate and commitment from these Staveley players could not be faulted - and whilst they will be disappointed in conceding a late equaliser, they will take great heart from the overall performance. Staveley supporters were certainly impressed and cheered the whole team as they left the pitch.

Staveley took the lead with their first attack when Lee Growcock played Ryan Damms (left) in, 'Dammsy' making no mistake with his accurate left foot shot.

1-0

Staveley continued to enjoy good possession with full back Brad Jones and forward Martin Brissett particularly involved in most things.

Jones had a chance on the half hour mark after being set up by Chris Coy and soon after, Coy had his own great chance for a second goal but dragged his shot wide.

Heanor were not short of attacking ideas but time after time, they found experienced centre backs Todd Jordan and James Colliver in commanding form.

Jordan put in a 'Man of the Match' performance by showing great tenacity for the whole game, making numerous courageous tackles and generally not being afraid to use his head - or any other part of his body - to win back possession.

As half time approached, Staveley had a penalty claim turned down when Brad Jones went down under a tackle in the opponents' box, then Heanor had a couple of half chances which came to nothing.

Richard Ayres then had to make a great save from a close range shot following a corner.

HT: 1-0

The home side began the second half in much the same way as they played in the first, creating a great scoring chance in the first minute, although this time, a thunderous 35 yard shot from Ryan Damms came back off the post.

Staveley then played their best football of the match for the next 20 minutes and created numerous openings but were unable to score the vital second goal.

The closest they came was on 52 minutes when a Martin Brissett shot hit the bar and the rebound fell to Ryan Damms in front of goal, but his side-footed shot went wide when, in all honesty, it would have been easier to score!

The match became an end to end game and a great advert for non-league football.

Heanor enjoyed plenty of possession but strong defending by Staveley meant that goalkeeper Richard Ayres only had one save of note to make in the second half.

In midfield Scott Ellis worked hard to provide both defensive cover and also create width on the right hand side when Staveley attacked.

Staveley manager Billy Fox made his three substitutions in quick successionStaveley Manager Billy Fox (left) made his three substitutions in quick succession to bring on fresh legs and each player leaving the pitch was given a standing ovation by the crowd in recognition of their efforts.

Every Staveley player worked their socks off in the last 20 minutes, substitute Pat Lindley making a great saving tackle in the box to prevent a goal scoring chance.

And just when it looked like they were about to secure all three points, Staveley were undone on 82 minutes when Heanor's Jason Foster beat a defender and took the ball into the penalty area, placing his shot past Richard Ayres.

Both sides then pushed for the winning goal but neither could find the vital final touch.

FT: 1-1

Staveley will be delighted with the overall performance and will know that they created enough clear chances that on another day would have given them all three points.

The next game at Inkersall Road is on Saturday 9th February when Staveley host Parkgate, kick off 3pm.

Staveley Lineup:
Richard Ayres, Kyle Fores-Chambers, Brad Jones, James Colliver, Todd Jordan, Lee Growcock (Pat Linley, 66), Scott Ellis (Sam Finlaw, 71), Andrew Fox, Ryan Damms (c), Martin Brissett (Steve Mansell, 75), Chris Coy.

Subs not used: Carl Vickers, Josh Fields

Staveley scorers: Chris Coy

Staveley Man of the Match: Todd Jordan

Weather: (3° C) Dry, with an ice cold wind

Pitch: Average

Attendance: 106

 

Keep in touch with all the latest fixtures, news and even Video highlights at www.staveleyfc.co.uk

 

 

 

 

 

 

 

 

 

 

 

